<title>JORDAN: Jordan's March M1 money supply down 2 pct from Feb.</title>
<headline>Jordan's March M1 money supply down 2 pct from Feb.</headline>
<dateline>AMMAN 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan's broadly defined M1 money supply fell two percent to 1.559 billion dinars ($2.20 billion) in March from 1.592 billion in February, the Central Bank statistical bulletin said.</p>
<p>The March 1997 figure was nearly seven percent down on the 1.673 billion dinars in the same month last year.</p>
<p>				  (All figures in millions of dinars)</p>
<p>				  Mar 1997  Feb 1997     Mar 1996</p>
<p> Currency in circulation     972	 981	  1,032</p>
<p> Money Supply (M1)	   1,559     1,592	  1,673</p>
<p> Money Supply (M2)	   5,241     5,350	  5,165</p>
<p>----------------------- ANNUAL INDICATORS ----------------</p>
<p>				  (All figures in millions of dinars)</p>
<p>				  1996    1995    1994     1993</p>
<p> Currency in circulation  952     1,051   1,073    1,048</p>
<p> Money Supply (M1)	  1539    1,746   1,746    1,730</p>
<p> Money Supply (M2)	  5226    5,160   4,814    4,482</p>
<p>NOTE -- The Central Bank defines M1 and M2 as:</p>
<p>M1 - currency in circulation and dinar sight deposits.</p>
<p>M2 - currency in circulation, including demand deposits in dinars and deposits of municipalities, public entities and non-banking financial institutions.</p>
<p>$1=0.709 dinars</p>
<p>- Amman newsroom 962 623776</p>
